( F5 T4 U9c: a field quadratic in x, y and linear in z is represented
  exactly by the -prism12 {tria6 x 2-node line}. All nodes prescribed
  u_x = 0.01 {x^2 + 0.5 x y} {1 + z}, u_y = u_z = 0; E 1, nu 0. Analytic:
  post_point disx at (0.25, 0.25, 0.5), (0.5, 0.25, 0.25), (0.1, 0.6, 0.75) =
  1.40625e-3, 3.90625e-3, 7e-4 {point_el.cc}; at every one of the 14
  integration points sigxx = 0.01 {2 x + 0.5 y} {1 + z} and
  sigxz = 0.005 {x^2 + 0.5 x y}. The Professional 02-08-2026 {run with
  -minimal, its default rule stops} interpolates post_point differently:
  5e-3, 7.5e-3, 2e-3 for u_x = 0.01 x^2 {1 + z} instead of 9.375e-4,
  3.125e-3, 1.75e-4 [DIVERGENCES PRISM12-POST-POINT]. )
echo -no
